⚠️ Potential issue | 🟡 Minor | ⚡ Quick win
Text limit is enforced in bytes, not characters.
The issue specifies a 65,535 character limit, but len(o.Text) returns the byte count. Multibyte UTF-8 text under the character limit can be wrongly rejected. If the intent is a character cap, count runes instead.

🐛 Proposed fix to count characters
-	maxLength := 65535
-	if len(o.Text) > maxLength {
+	maxLength := 65535
+	if utf8.RuneCountInString(o.Text) > maxLength {
 		return NewAppError("CommandResponse.IsValid", "model.command_response.is_valid.text.app_error", nil, "text is too long", http.StatusBadRequest)
 	}
Add the import:
 import (
 	"encoding/json"
 	"io"
 	"net/http"
 	"strings"
+	"unicode/utf8"

 	"github.com/mattermost/mattermost/server/public/utils"
 )

Note: if the 65,535 cap is actually a downstream byte-storage limit, the current len() check is correct—please confirm which constraint applies.


📝 Committable suggestion

‼️ IMPORTANT
Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.




